{
    "word": "ratfink",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1020d72d-2a84-36cb-89a2-1393d8fc96cb",
                "word": "ratfink",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac531843-96dc-4e5b-a48e-2342f01faacd",
                        "entry_id": "1020d72d-2a84-36cb-89a2-1393d8fc96cb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ratfinks"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                        "entry_id": "1020d72d-2a84-36cb-89a2-1393d8fc96cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An informer or spy; a traitor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1c890ab-1422-490d-8f4d-8e4bfe9d8fd6",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "The authors have facetiously labeled the contemplated musical as 'Ratfink', after the name of its central character, James J. Ratfink. Its title is not meant in a derogatory sense."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02cd9c14-7096-4f49-a712-65231c5664c8",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "The film director accused him of being the worst kind of a rat fink (rat pack talk) for leaving a play so early."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12817e95-56ce-407d-91a8-daa9c0babe4c",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "The first factor is labeled the \"Ratfink\" factor. This factor consists only of items that measure whether a boy would give information to various adult figures if one of his friends were in trouble."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac6a5cba-2852-4677-90c0-2dbb9d101382",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "In my novella, \"Our Lady of Desperation,\" a painter and civil servant square up to one another. […] One of the protagonists was an artist; so it was assumed I was somehow in his camp. In fact both are ratfinks; when thieves fall out, honest men, if they don't come into their dues, are at least afforded a wry smile."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f9a70cd-f895-4458-b261-6a0afbc53548",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "You'd think that some rat-fink in the company would spill the beans and warn Mr. Wright, but nobody did. There wasn't much company loyalty at Nineveh Publishing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f2b6f3d-3841-4213-8ec2-82d49e8e205d",
                                "sense_id": "94b2bf09-6cf1-3e57-9ad8-8829a5f7f1cc",
                                "text": "He wasn't a gabber, nor a squawker not a ratfink nor a snitch. He wasn't a whistleblower. He wasn't a gossip. He didn't talk about someone behind their back. Banks knew that firsthand because he had tried on several occasions to get Quinley to talk about other people, and Quinley would never do it. He'd laugh and change the subject."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0dfabd45-a1ee-3d70-b996-641a0bce1e02",
                        "entry_id": "1020d72d-2a84-36cb-89a2-1393d8fc96cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dislikable or contemptible person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US",
                            "also",
                            "attributive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b7a3643-7763-4280-9e77-ab20f18319b3",
                                "sense_id": "0dfabd45-a1ee-3d70-b996-641a0bce1e02",
                                "text": "Maxwell—or Maxie, as he was familiarly called by his once and former rat fink girlfriend—lived in a six-story walkup on a narrow street in Calm's Point, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7198347-bab7-4973-9e76-2a165b34138a",
                                "sense_id": "0dfabd45-a1ee-3d70-b996-641a0bce1e02",
                                "text": "He [Dubyaman, a parody comic superhero based loosely on George W. Bush] searches for \"dirty ratfink terrorists\" and aims to ferret out their \"whacko ideas.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fdaff3a-403e-494d-9428-0d08d8e04083",
                                "sense_id": "0dfabd45-a1ee-3d70-b996-641a0bce1e02",
                                "text": "I started not to write the sad story of what happened to these two outstanding soldiers because I didn't want to convey the mistaken impression that the ratfinks they ran into were typical of the fine soldiers who fought in Vietnam."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf2280a7-a651-4ab9-930c-27a550f247ea",
                                "sense_id": "0dfabd45-a1ee-3d70-b996-641a0bce1e02",
                                "text": "'What did you just do?' Sunshine asked. 'Did you just kill a moth?' / 'No,' he said. He glanced at it then flicked it off. Shimmering dust filmed his skin. […] / 'Sometimes you are such a ratfink jackass,' she told him, throwing his hand down, some of the shimmery dust on her own fingers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c10827bd-fab4-4014-bfbc-9ecd3196e75e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1020d72d-2a84-36cb-89a2-1393d8fc96cb",
                        "source_sense_description": "informer or spy",
                        "target_lang_word": "шпио́н",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "шпио́н",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88bf4729-d957-3402-9e6a-6063004a1d35",
                                        "entry_id": "667d3fc1-fc88-3553-bbb1-4b392e14972f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "тот, кто занимается шпионажем; тайный агент иностранного государства"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "265fdbd5-d480-4521-8278-a0ed86f4be50",
                                                "sense_id": "88bf4729-d957-3402-9e6a-6063004a1d35",
                                                "text": "Казаки разыскивали японского шпиона, одетого русским военным врачом."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b084fa4-b6c0-386b-bd28-cf1431b8f467",
                                        "entry_id": "667d3fc1-fc88-3553-bbb1-4b392e14972f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "устар. полицейский агент по сыску, слежке за кем-либо; шпик"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdbd2ab6-90fd-4792-ae74-b5647b53d187",
                                                "sense_id": "9b084fa4-b6c0-386b-bd28-cf1431b8f467",
                                                "text": "Мы заметили, что за нами установлен систематический надзор тайной полиции. Для надзора за обеими квартирами были поставлены два шпиона."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87515c5b-5735-3812-9186-bee45f1dff23",
                                        "entry_id": "667d3fc1-fc88-3553-bbb1-4b392e14972f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "разг., сниж. тот, кто следит за кем-либо, выслеживает кого-либо, доносит на кого-либо"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fd0f3bf-3eb3-3f69-9b67-d3eec192fc30",
                                        "entry_id": "667d3fc1-fc88-3553-bbb1-4b392e14972f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "советск. необоснованное обвинение в годы сталинских репрессий: тот, кто якобы занимается шпионажем, является тайным агентом иностранного государства"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
